===Verb===
{{en-verb|hit<,,hit> on}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[flirt]] with; to [[approach]] and speak to (someone), seeking [[romance]], [[love]], [[sex]], etc.
#: {{synonyms|en|proposition|come on|pass|make a pass}}
#: {{ux|en|That's the third guy that has '''hit on''' her tonight.}}
#: {{ux|en|Guys are '''hitting on''' them almost all the time.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=Sep 23 2003|author=Bill Amend|title=FoxTrot|genre=comic|passage=''Don Iguan'': I have slithered the world over in search of beauty such as yours! Perhaps you'd like to come back to my lair this evening. I'll light some candles... put on some beetle music... <br />''Mom'': I'm married. Go '''hit on''' your sister.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Sheila Roberts|title=A Wedding on Primrose Street|publisher=MIRA|year=2015|page=181|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/weddingonprimros0000robe/page/181/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-7783-1815-6|passage=Anne watched as he put an arm around one of the bridesmaids and gave her a decidedly ungrandfatherly squeeze while attempting to look down her dress, then proceeded to '''hit on''' the mother of the groom.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[discover]], [[pinpoint]]; to [[think up]]; to [[realize]].
#: {{ux|en|He '''hit on''' a great idea for improving the design.}}
#: {{ux|en|I think you've just '''hit''' right '''on''' the solution.}}
# {{&lit|en}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Global Journal on Human Rights Law|year=1996|page=210|passage=He was '''hit on''' his head so strongly that he stumbled forward and then he was severely hit from several sides.}}

